<title>HUNGARY: PANNON-VALTO SWINGS TO H1 OP PROFIT.</title>
<headline>PANNON-VALTO SWINGS TO H1 OP PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-months ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating result	  34.0 profit vs    18.1 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	    86.6	  vs   100.7</p>
<p>    Net sales		    0.0	  vs     0.9 (*)</p>
<p>    Other revenue	     74.8	  vs    16.0</p>
<p>    Material expenditures    1.4	  vs     1.9</p>
<p>    Personnel expenditures   7.5	  vs     8.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 0.4	  vs     2.0</p>
<p>    Other costs		  8.1	  vs    12.1</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	23.3	  vs    10.5</p>
<p>    Net financial income    52.6 profit vs   118.8 profit</p>
<p>     Financial revenue     114.6	  vs   130.7</p>
<p>     Financial expend.	62.0	  vs    11.9</p>
<p>NOTE -(*) Pannon-Valto Rt is an investment company, therefore it has not sales-type revenues. The figures are unaudited and were calculated in accordance with Hungarian Accounting Standards.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
